{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review deportation laws for foreign domestic abuse offenders & victim protection",
        "additional_details": "We believe we need stronger laws, prompt decisions, accountability and effective communication to ensure risks are assessed and victims and children are protected. This should include lawful notification to the victim of the offender\u2019s detention, release and decisions about their accommodation. Despite non molestation orders, victims can face fear and uncertainty. Victims should not have to chase agencies for reassurance.",
        "background": "We call for an urgent review to look at how deportation laws can be strengthened for foreign domestic abuse offenders including how to speed up decisions, hold authorities accountable for delays, improve agency communication, and protect victims with mandatory risk assessments and communication.",
